paths: file:std/parsing/regex.ssc file:std/parsing/combinators.ssc file:v3/regex-subset-gate.sh file:tests/conformance/regex-subset.ssc file:tests/conformance/expected/regex-subset.txt file:.github/workflows/v3.yml file:BUGS.md
scope: |
  Layer 2 of v3-extension-unblocks-two-files-into-a-lane-DIFF: `PRegex` was answered by the HOST
  (java.util.regex, through a native string method), so each lane got its own engine's dialect and
  v3's executor had no answer at all. Replaced by a prefix matcher written in ScalaScript —
  std/parsing/regex.ssc — so every lane that runs programs runs the same one.

  Not layer 1. The executor's missing `map` on a Parser value (an extension shadowed by a built-in
  name) is a separate defect and is NOT touched here.

  Paths beyond the first four, added after planning: the conformance expectation file the runner
  requires, v3.yml to register the new gate, and BUGS.md for the entry. BUGS.md is co-held with
  rust-unresolved-names and v3-toplevel-val-env — edits anchor on this entry's own heading.
next: register v3/regex-subset-gate.sh in v3.yml, corpus A/B, then release
